# oracle: pair_style meam, single element Cu-like synthetic entry (w12meam_lib.meam + w12meam.meam, zbl 0), 2x2x2 fcc cell (32 atoms), 0.05 A sinusoidal displacement, velocities from atom-style variables, fix nve, 50 steps of 0.001 ps
# oracle: cutoff window. rc = 4.0 and delr = 0.1, so the radial smoothing window is [3.9, 4.0]. The cutoff form is not verified inside that window, so the case keeps every pair distance out of it: fcc shells sit at 2.556 (NN), 3.615 and 4.43 A; 0.05 A displacements move a pair distance by <= 0.17 A, and the speeds (<= 0.5 A/ps) move atoms by <= 0.025 A over 50 steps, so the 2nd shell stays in [3.4, 3.85] A and the 3rd shell is above 4.2 A
# oracle-inputs: w12meam_lib.meam w12meam.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-6 abs=1e-10
# oracle-tolerance: rel=1e-6 is needed for press only. Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the native press and the native finite-difference pressure from its own energy agree to 6e-4 bar, and the engine's agree to 4e-4 bar; the native press differs from the engine's by 4e-4 bar at step 0 (1e-7 relative), with differences up to 7e-4 bar over 50 steps. pe agrees to 2e-11 relative at step 0 and 3e-10 abs at step 50.
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 3.615
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 63.546
variable        dx atom 0.05*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.05*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.05*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.4*cos(1.7*y-0.6*z)
variable        vy atom 0.4*sin(1.2*z+0.9*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*cos(2.1*x-0.8*y+0.2)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w12meam_lib.meam Cu w12meam.meam Cu
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             50
